<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · West Africa</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Ketu</h1><p class="st-meta">1500 CE – 1886 CE (approx.) · capital Ketu</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Ancient Yoruba kingdom on today's Benin-Nigeria border, a Yoruba outpost between the Oyo and Dahomey powers.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Ketu traditions trace its royal line, the Alaketu, to a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oduduwa">Oduduwa</a> who left <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-ife">Ile-Ife</a>, and name Ede as the founder of the walled town of Ketu. The kingdom took shape in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba</a> lands, and its massive town wall and gate, the Idena, became symbols of its antiquity.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The Alaketu was chosen from royal houses in rotation and ruled with town chiefs and powerful religious societies. Ketu was a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yoruba">Yoruba</a> religion, notably of the orisha cults later carried to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/new-republic-brazil">Brazil</a>. Lying between the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/oyo-empire">Oyo Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-dahomey">Kingdom of Dahomey</a>, it was repeatedly raided by Dahomean armies from the late 18th century.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1886 the forces of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-dahomey">Dahomey</a> under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glele">Glele</a> destroyed Ketu and carried off much of its population. After the French conquest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-dahomey">Dahomey</a> the town was resettled within <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-dahomey">French Dahomey</a>, and the Alaketu still reigns at Ketou in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1500 CE – 1886 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78